UI.en.privacyNote='🔒 Privacy: this page does not collect identifying information such as your name, email, phone number or precise location, and your favourites stay in your own browser. To understand which parts are actually useful it does send anonymous usage data — which places you open, which features you use, the text you type into the search box (digit runs stripped and truncated, so it shows what people look for rather than an address), the domain of whatever site linked you here (the domain only, never the full address), which of three buckets your screen falls into (phone / tablet / desktop — just those three values, so layout problems can be traced to a screen size), and whether the page was opened in a browser or installed to your home screen. It also uses a random identifier generated locally in your browser; it is stored there and stays the same on your next visit so return use can be told apart, but it is not linked to any identity and does not track you across sites or devices. No cookies are set and no IP address is recorded on the server. You can inspect every one of these requests in full in your browser\'s DevTools Network panel (/api/event). Two other third parties receive a request when the page loads: the map-imagery tile server (currently MapTiler, api.maptiler.com; Esri, server.arcgisonline.com, if it is unavailable), and Cloudflare Web Analytics (static.cloudflareinsights.com — no cookies, no individual tracking, aggregate visit counts only). Both see your IP address in the process; for the map that is the same as any web map. Offline, everything but the imagery still works. If you tap the Near Me button, your browser will ask for location permission; your coordinates are used only on your own device to centre the map — they are never sent to our server or logged.';
